{
 "_what": "Why xG coverage must be sampled ACROSS a season, not from the most recent fixtures. Two probes of the same leagues on the same day, differing only in which completed fixtures were sampled.",
 "_finding": "A most-recent-3 sample called Bundesliga, Primeira Liga and Ligue 1 'partial' and J1 'absent'. A 6-sample spread evenly across the same seasons showed Bundesliga/Primeira/Ligue 1 fully covered in every regular-season round, with the ONLY miss being the round labelled 'Final' — the promotion/relegation playoff, which sits in a distinct, later-created provider fixture-id block (154xxxx) and carries no xG. J1 is genuinely partial (4/6), missing one regular-season round and a '7th place' playoff. Reporting those three leagues as xG-less would have been wrong, and the error was entirely in the sampling.",
 "_consequence": "apifootball.measure_coverage uses spread_sample() and stores sampling_method='spread_across_season'. It also records miss_rounds, so a partial verdict is attributable to a round rather than left as a bare percentage.",
